# Optional in dev — the Vite dev server proxies relative "/api/..."
# requests to the backend (see vite.config.ts), which is what makes LAN
# testing (opening the app from a phone on the same Wi-Fi) work without
# editing this file per network.
#
# Only set this in dev if you're NOT using the proxy — e.g. pointing the
# built frontend at a backend hosted somewhere else:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.23:5000/api

# --- Production ---
# You have two options; pick one. Whichever you use, this is a BUILD-TIME
# value baked into the JS bundle — set it in your hosting platform's
# environment variable settings (not in a committed .env file), and
# rebuild whenever it changes.
#
# Option A (recommended): leave VITE_API_BASE_URL unset and configure an
# "/api/*" rewrite to your backend at the hosting-platform level instead
# (see vercel.json / netlify.toml in this folder). The app keeps calling
# a relative "/api" path, the platform forwards it to your backend
# server-side, and — importantly — this keeps the admin login cookie
# working, since the browser sees everything as one origin.
#
# Option B: point directly at your deployed backend's full URL:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com/api
# Simpler to set up, but the admin session cookie is then a genuinely
# cross-site cookie — see the deployment report for why that needs a
# backend-side change (sameSite: "none"; secure: true) this phase
# deliberately did NOT make.
